{"type":"match","data":{"path":{"text":"www.in.gov/Sidebar__docid_21822.txt"},"lines":{"text":"In 1949, NBA coach Gregg Popovich was born in East Chicago. He played basketball at Merrillville High School before playing and coaching for the U.S. Air Force Academy's basketball team. He became the head coach of the San Antonio Spurs in 1996. He led the Spurs to five NBA Championships (1999, 2003, 2005, 2007, and 2014). Additionally, Popovich won the NBA Coach of the Year Award three times (2003, 2012, and 2014), and led Team USA to a Gold Medal in the 2020 Olympics in Tokyo. (Lake Co.)\n"},"line_number":255,"absolute_offset":54068,"submatches":[{"match":{"text":"Air Force Academy"},"start":150,"end":167}]}}
